This seems (along with the issue of not having iplots loaded) as one  
of the issues that have been addressed in the most recent development  
version. Please try
install.packages(c("JGR","JavaGD","iplots"),,"http://rforge.net/")

A new release should be out in the next few days.


> Also: if I start R from a directory in which I have an .RData file,  
> and then start JGR() from within R, should not the default directory  
> be the one from which I started R?

JGR() is just an alias for starting the JGR script, so it will behave  
exactly as R - i.e. the workspace is restored from the directory you  
started it in. I'm not sure what you mean by "default directory" but  
the working directory is set according to your preferences. If you  
don't want the directory to be changed, use ".".

I agree that we could have some discussion about the startup - it  
would be nice to have consistent interpretation of the settings, e.g.  
to use the working directory preference for the workspace as well. It  
may be worth changing.


> Also, I think that the .RData is not automatically read in JGR?

It is:
[...]
Type 'demo()' for some demos, 'help()' for on-line help, or
'help.start()' for an HTML browser interface to help.
Type 'q()' to quit R.

[Previously saved workspace restored]


> what about the .history ? I'm confused with this.
>

I'm not aware of .history, but JGR uses .JGRhistory to keep console  
history. However, there seems to be a problem with the startup -  
apparently it always loads .JGRhistory regardless of the working  
directory. IMHO that needs to be fixed.

Thanks for your report,
Simon

