You are specifying the encoding (see the corresponding R  
documentation), so it's up to you to choose the one that works best  
for your data. The only exception is the Rserve configuration file  
which is parsed before R is started (and thus before the locale is set  
up), but that should still work as long as you use encoding used by  
the system.

If you want more detailed help, please tell us exactly what you are  
trying to do, which OS, R, Rserve and what locale are you using -  
sessionInfo() output helps there as well.

